.\" Man page for z_privesc
.\" Generated for Z-Privesc 1.0.0
.TH Z_PRIVESC 1 "2026-06-04" "1.0.0" "Z-Privesc Manual"
.SH NAME
z_privesc \- privilege-escalation audit tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B z_privesc
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBZ\-Privesc\fR inspects a Linux system for misconfigurations known
to enable local privilege escalation across seventeen categories:
SUID binaries, writable PATH entries, Linux capabilities, writable
authentication files in \fI/etc\fR, exposed Docker control sockets,
polkit / pkexec weaknesses, world\-writable sensitive files, kernel
version matches against well\-known privilege\-escalation CVEs, cron
misconfiguration, sudoers rule audit, SSH private key permissions,
privileged group membership, systemd unit file audit, kernel
hardening /proc/sys settings, root process binary audit, NFS export
misconfiguration, and LD_PRELOAD / ld.so.conf audit.

Every finding is collected as a piece of \fIevidence\fR and evaluated
by the \fITruthimatics Public Version\fR engine, which assigns a
majority\-weighted \fIverdict\fR to the chain (DETERMINISTIC,
UNCERTAIN, or REJECT) and a CVSS\-like \fIrisk score\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Run every registered probe.  This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-probe=\fINAME\fR
Run only the named probe.  May be repeated to run a subset.
Recognised names are:
.RS
.IP
suid, writable_path, capabilities, writable_etc, docker_socket,
polkit, world_writable, kernel_vuln, cron, sudoers, ssh_keys,
groups, service, kernel_hardening, process, nfs, ld_preload
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-root=\fIDIR\fR
Treat \fIDIR\fR as the filesystem root.  Useful for scanning the
rootfs of a stopped container.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a JSON audit report conforming to schema
\fIz-privesc.audit/v1\fR on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-html
Emit an HTML audit report on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress progress output.  Errors continue to be logged to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable debug\-level logging.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the build ID and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
No privilege\-escalation paths were identified.
.TP
.B 1
A probe encountered a fatal error (filesystem failure, permission
denied).
.TP
.B 2
At least one probe reported a DETERMINISTIC finding.
.TP
.B 125
Internal error (out of memory, argument validation, ...).
.SH OUTPUT SCHEMA
The JSON document produced with \fB\-\-json\fR conforms to schema
\fIz-privesc.audit/v1\fR.  Each probe produces a record with the
chain verdict, the evidence count, a risk score, and an array of
findings.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATH
Consulted by the \fIwritable_path\fR probe.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/self/status
Read by the \fIcapabilities\fR probe to determine the process
capability bounding set.
.TP
.I /proc/version
Read by the \fIkernel_vuln\fR probe.
.TP
.I /var/run/docker.sock
Inspected by the \fIdocker_socket\fR probe.
.TP
.I /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow, /etc/sudoers
Inspected by the \fIwritable_etc\fR probe.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run every probe and emit JSON:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fB
z_privesc \-\-all \-\-json | jq
\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run only the SUID and kernel probes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fB
z_privesc \-\-probe=suid \-\-probe=kernel_vuln \-\-json
\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Scan a stopped container's rootfs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fB
z_privesc \-\-root=/var/lib/containerd/.../rootfs \-\-json
\fR
.fi
.RE
